          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            In the context of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/schemes"} schemes
            there is a traditional notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+morphism+of+schemes"} étale morphism of schemes
            and an
            %em étale topos
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} category of sheaves
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+site"} étale site
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covers"} covers
            by such
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+morphism+of+schemes"} étale morphisms
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#EtaleToposOfAScheme"}> Étale topos of a scheme
              \.
          %p
            More abstractly, given that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+morphisms+of+schemes"} étale morphisms of schemes
            may be characterized as modal morphisms with respect to an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+shape+modality"} infinitesimal shape modality
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohesion"} differential cohesion
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#GeneralAbstract"} Étale topos of a differentially cohesive object
          %h3#EtaleToposOfAScheme Étale topos of a scheme
          %p
            An
            %strong étale topos
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
            over an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+site"} étale site
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+morphisms"} étale morphisms
            into the base
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            of an étale
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+cohomology"} étale cohomology
          %p
            More generally there is the pro-étale topos over a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pro-%C3%A9tale+site"} pro-étale site
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            of a pro-étale
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            includes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weil+cohomology+theory"} Weil cohomology theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%84%93-adic+cohomology"} ℓ-adic cohomology
          %p
            Generally, given that an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+morphism+of+schemes"} étale morphism of schemes
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+%C3%A9tale+morphism"} formally étale morphism
            subject to a size constraint on its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
            – for an actual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+morphism+of+schemes"} étale morphism of schemes
            the fibers are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+sets"} finite sets
            in the suitable sense (formal duals to
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+algebras"} étale algebras
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pro-%C3%A9tale+morphism+of+schemes"} pro-étale morphism of schemes
            they are
