          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EtaleDescentDetectedOnOpenImmersionCovers"}
              we are reduced to showing that the represented presheaf satisfies
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
              along collections of open immersions and along surjective maps of affines. For the first this is clear (it is
              = succeed "-descent)." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zariski+topology"} Zariski topology
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/faithfully+flat"} faithfully flat
              cover of affines
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(B) \to Spec(A)
              it follows with the exactness of the correspomnding
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Amitsur+complex"} Amitsur complex
          .num_remark
