          %h3#relation_to_zariski_topos Relation to Zariski topos
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_5 Remark
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover"} cover
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zariski+topology"} Zariski topology
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/schemes"} schemes
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+immersion+of+schemes"} open immersion of schemes
              and hence is in particular an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+morphism+of+schemes"} étale morphism of schemes
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+site"} étale site
              is finer than the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zariski+site"} Zariski site
              and so every étale
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
              is a Zariski sheaf, but not necessarily conversely. Expressed in a different way, the étale topos is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subtopos"} subtopos
              of the Zariski topos.
          %p
            For more see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "etale+cohomology#RelationZariskiEtaleCohomology"} étale cohomology – Properties – Relation to Zariski cohomology
          %h3#as_a_classifying_topos As a classifying topos
          %p
            The étale topos over the big étale site of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+rings"} commutative rings
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+topos"} classifying topos
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+local+rings"} strict local rings
